# Apt sources used to build the nfsroot and the mirror embedded in the ISO.
# The apt sources of an installed system come from elsewhere: fai-cd writes the
# mirror location of the CD, and images built with fai-diskimage take
# files/etc/apt/sources.list/SEAPATH_RAW from the config space.
#
# This file holds the debootstrap suite alone. Every other repository belongs in
# sources.list.d: while fai-mirror downloads the packages of base-pkgs.lis, it
# replaces this file with a "deb <mirror> <suite> main" line rebuilt from
# FAI_DEBOOTSTRAP and leaves sources.list.d untouched. A repository listed here
# is therefore invisible for the base packages, which are exactly the ones no
# other package depends on (they are Essential), so they would be fetched from
# the plain suite while their tightly versioned dependencies come from the
# security suite. Such a mirror is not installable.

deb http://ftp.fr.debian.org/debian trixie main contrib non-free non-free-firmware
